\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{\code{HasComposites P} is existence of the required opcartesian universal cells, including specified treatment of the empty path. When the hypotheses hold, construct a double Segal nerve by coherent diagrams of paths and composite witnesses. Prove that its witness choices are contractible and that it has the relevant invariance and comparison with a double ∞-category model. This is a construction, not restriction along an assumed inclusion of \code{Δ×Δ} into the virtual arity category.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{A virtual path can have many horizontal arrows but no specified composite.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{Obtaining a double nerve merely by saying horizontal composites exist.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{\ref{at-ft-0004}: comparison with the precisely named Ruit model after any required completion; \ref{at-ft-0005}: ordinary profunctor coends and their classical double category.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{provisional. The set-level instance precedes the full ∞-comparison.}
}
